  "title": "Cyrus the Great",
  "summary": "Cyrus II of Persia founded the Achaemenid Empire. He reigned from 559 to 530 BCE, took Media by about 550, defeated Croesus of Lydia, and conquered Babylonia in 539, after which Judean exiles were allowed to return home. He died campaigning against the Massagetae. His mausoleum stands at Pasargadae, the capital he founded.",
